[{"slug": "west-virginia-property-tax-guide", "title": "West Virginia Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>West Virginia Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in West Virginia</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>West Virginia Property Tax Guide: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a West Virginia Property Tax Guide sale</li><li>Turn the West Virginia Property Tax Guide offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a West Virginia House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>West Virginia property tax is assessed and collected at the local level, and owners can appeal an assessment.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>The county commission meets as a board of equalization and review no later than February 1 of the tax year and may adjourn sine die any time after February 15, and must adjourn by the last day of February. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-24; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-24/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The board fixes property at 60 percent of true and actual value if assessed above or below that, and no assessment may exceed 60 percent of true and actual value. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-24; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-24/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>An assessment may not be increased without at least five days&#x27; written notice to the taxpayer. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-24; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-24/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A person who fails to apply for relief at the board meeting waives the right to seek correction for the current year except on appeal to the Office of Tax Appeals or as otherwise provided. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-24; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-24/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A taxpayer who elects a hearing before the Board of Equalization and Review may appeal the board&#x27;s order to the Office of Tax Appeals; the taxpayer&#x27;s standard of proof is a preponderance of the evidence. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-24; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-24/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>An Office of Tax Appeals petition from a valuation or a Board of Equalization and Review order must be filed by March 31 of the property tax year or it is dismissed as untimely. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-25b; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-25B/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>An appeal of a Tax Commissioner ruling on taxability or classification must be filed within 30 days after written notice of the ruling. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-25b; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-25B/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The former circuit-court relief section for erroneous assessments, \u00a711-3-25, is marked repealed. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-3-25; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-3-25/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>West Virginia sells tax liens at public auction; unsold tracts may be sold by the Auditor without further advertising or auction. (W. Va. Code \u00a711A-3-2; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11A-3-2/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>After a tax lien sale, the owner or a lienholder may redeem at any time before a tax deed is issued. (W. Va. Code \u00a711A-3-56; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11A-3-56/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in West Virginia?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy West Virginia houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-homestead-exemption/'>West Virginia Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-estate-tax/'>West Virginia Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-west-virginia/'>We buy houses in West Virginia</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://tax.wv.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia State Tax Department</a></li><li><a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia Code</a></li><li><a href='https://www.courtswv.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia Judiciary</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for West Virginia Property Tax Guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"West Virginia\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-west-virginia/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"West Virginia Property Tax Guide: Appeals\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-property-tax-guide/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "West Virginia Property Tax Guide: Appeals", "rank_math_description": "West Virginia property tax: appeals, exemptions, delinquent tax and selling a house with tax due. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "west virginia property tax"}, {"slug": "west-virginia-homestead-exemption", "title": "West Virginia Homestead Exemption: Eligibility, Filing and Selling the Home", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>West Virginia Homestead Exemption: Eligibility, Filing and Selling the Home</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in West Virginia</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>West Virginia Homestead Exemption: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a West Virginia Homestead Exemption sale</li><li>Turn the West Virginia Homestead Exemption offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a West Virginia House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>West Virginia offers property tax relief for qualifying homeowners, and official sources explain the rules.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Exemption from ad valorem property tax applies to the first $20,000 of assessed value of an owner-occupied homestead used exclusively for residential purposes. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-3; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-3/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The owner must be 65 or older or certified permanently and totally disabled, and a West Virginia resident for the two consecutive calendar years before the tax year (with stated exceptions). (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-3; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-3/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The exemption attaches to the homestead occupied on the July 1 assessment date and applies to taxes for the following tax year. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-3; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-3/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If the homestead is transferred by deed, will or otherwise, the $20,000 exemption is removed on the next July 1 assessment date unless the new owner qualifies. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-3; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-3/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A claim must be filed with the county assessor on or before December 1 following the July 1 assessment day; missing it waives the exemption for the next tax year. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-4; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-4/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A claimant aged 65 or older need not refile after the first claim unless moving to a new homestead. (W. Va. Code \u00a711-6B-4; <a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/11-6B-4/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in West Virginia?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy West Virginia houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-property-tax-guide/'>West Virginia Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-estate-tax/'>West Virginia Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-west-virginia/'>We buy houses in West Virginia</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://tax.wv.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia State Tax Department</a></li><li><a href='https://code.wvlegislature.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia Code</a></li><li><a href='https://www.courtswv.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>West Virginia Judiciary</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for West Virginia Homestead Exemption, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"West Virginia\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-west-virginia/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"West Virginia Homestead Exemption Guide\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/west-virginia-homestead-exemption/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "West Virginia Homestead Exemption Guide", "rank_math_description": "West Virginia homestead exemption: who qualifies, how to apply and what happens when you sell. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "west virginia homestead exemption"}, {"slug": "west-virginia-estate-tax", "title": "West Virginia Estate and Inheritance Tax: What Heirs Owe When Selling", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-